Email templates Needed:
*Updated 2026-10-12 to match the Harbor design. The design is the source of truth.*

Cancelation from Coach
Cancellation from client to coach — only inside the notice period (ADR-009, Kim 2026-10-08). *2026-11-13 (G-38): one
  email per cancellation, listing every late lesson in it.*
  *From ADR-009 decision 9 (moved 2026-11-08):* email templates required: cancellation from coach (to client), and
    cancellation from client (to coach). Phase 2: distinct templates by reason — sick, emergency, vacation.
  One message per family per cancellation (not one per lesson), because it is one decision that happened to touch
    several lessons. Messages state that the lesson is cancelled and offer a link to book a different time.
  Text form (Phase 2 for texts to families; ADR-007 amended 2026-10-12): one 160-character message, pointing at the
    email.
  Coach's text when a family cancels late (MVP, opt-in, decided by the owner 2026-09-30): one message, no free text, a
    pointer to the email. Because it goes to the coach rather than from them, it opens "BladeBook:" rather than the
    coach's own name — "BladeBook: Mia R. cancelled Tue 14 Oct 4:00pm. See email." The student's name is shortened to
    fit like any other variable field. (Opt-in rules: cancelation.md, "Coach told about a client cancellation".)
Phase 2: "Just booked" — a family booked just as the coach's schedule change cancelled that time (ADR-008, amended 2026-10-08).
Pending student declined by the coach (ADR-002 decision 2b).
*Changed 2026-10-20 (ADR-033 d6): the two shared-lesson warnings and "Shared lesson expired, skater not yet accepted"
  moved to Phase 2 (below). Only a skater the coach has already accepted can be invited, so nothing waits on the coach.*
*Changed 2026-11-13 by the owner (G-38): every shared-lesson email below is one per invitation or answer, listing
  every date it covers, not one per date. A four-week shared series sends one invitation, one "joined" to each family,
  one "declined" or "withdrawn", and, when the other family stops the series, one "keep or cancel" listing each date
