*In the Harbor design's email list (C_Coach Email Templates.md) and not above:*
Booking confirmation — to the family, when they book.
Day-of reminder — to the family, the morning of each lesson day.
  ~~Reminders are per lesson, not per client. Every scheduled lesson produces its own reminder. A client with two
  children who both have lessons on the same day receives two reminders, one per lesson. There is no per-client
  digest, no grouping, and no deduplication.~~ *(from ADR-002 decision 7, moved 2026-11-08)*
  *Changed 2026-11-13 by the owner (G-37):* one email per family per day, listing each of that day's lessons (skater,
  time, length, rink, and who it's shared with). A family with two children skating that day gets one email naming
  both. A family with lessons from two coaches that day gets one from each coach, since each comes from its coach
  and replies go to that coach.
Payment reminder — to the family, after a lesson is checked in. Includes the coach's payment instructions, and handles if switched on.
  It states the specific amount owed for that lesson, in the lesson's currency — not "payment is due"; a number —
  plus the coach's payment instructions. For a shared lesson the amount is the skater's share. One email per
  lesson: a family with two children checked in on the same day gets two reminders, each with its own amount.
  *(from ADR-003 §7, moved 2026-11-08)* The Phase 2 text-message version only states the amount and points at
  this email (see SMS Messages.md).
Schedule change — to the family, when a schedule save cancels or re-prices their lessons. Always sent.
Daily report — to the coach, every evening at 9 PM. *Phase 2 (owner, 2026-11-11)*: not sent in MVP. The wording below
  stands for when it ships. Until then, an unrecorded lesson shows as *Not recorded* on Payments and the lesson
  list, and as "attendance not recorded" in the weekly unpaid reminder.
  The report names the pending students and says what to do. *Added 2026-09-30, in place of a push notification
  the owner declined:* the email lists each pending student and lesson, with "No attendance recorded. If you
  recorded these on the rinkside app, open it with signal to send them; otherwise record them on the lesson list."
  It is the coach's nightly prompt for both a phone that never reconnected and a lesson nobody recorded.
  *(from ADR-014 §7, moved 2026-11-08)*
Unpaid lessons — to the coach, weekly on Monday morning.
  *Accepted 2026-09-30 (ADR-018).* One email per coach, not one per lesson, listing every past lesson still
  unpaid that is older than the threshold: 7 days (owner, 2026-11-12). Wording (owner, 2026-11-12, R10a):
  "You have unpaid lessons from more than [threshold] ago. Please mark each one as paid or waived." — followed
  by the list (date, time, skater, amount), and a link to the payment dashboard.
  A lesson with no recorded outcome says so in the list — "attendance not recorded" — because the coach may need
  to correct attendance on the lesson list before deciding whether it is owed.
  It covers every unpaid past lesson, whatever its attendance, including no-shows. A no-show is listed at
  ~~its full lesson price~~ what that skater owes (their share; the full price unless the lesson is shared;
  owner, 2026-11-12, R10c), labelled as a no-show, matching the dashboard. *(Corrected 2026-09-30: this first
  said a no-show "is not charged" in MVP, which misstated the rule.)*
  Phase 2: chargeable late cancellations are listed too, labelled as late fees.
  ~~Each lesson is listed once, when it crosses the threshold. Whether it should be listed again is open (ADR-018).~~
  A lesson is listed every Monday until it is marked paid or waived (owner, 2026-11-12; ADR-018 amendment).
  *(from ADR-018 §1 and §4, moved 2026-11-08)*
