To the coach:
Morning email — to the coach, around 7 AM on days with lessons: the rinkside link first, then today's lessons. Sent by the
  day-of reminder job; the on/off switch is Phase 2. Sent to the coach's login email, like the ~~daily report~~ *weekly unpaid reminder*. (ADR-023,
  2026-10-13; address decided 2026-10-15)
  Owner, 2026-10-13: a link at the top of this email is one of the two ways the coach reaches the rinkside page (the
  other is the large link on the coach website's Today page), so neither a home-screen icon nor a bookmark is needed.
  It goes to each coach with lessons that day and lists them, with the rinkside link first. A coach with no lessons
  that day gets no email. The link is a plain address; the page asks the coach to sign in as usual. MVP has no off
  switch; turning it off arrives with the email templates page in Phase 2. This adopts Kim's "daily email about
  lessons scheduled" (docs/Talking with Kim:.md.md).
  Owner, 2026-10-15: it goes to the coach's login email, the same verified address as the daily report, not the
  business email on the profile. The weekly unpaid-lesson reminder already goes there (ADR-018).
  *(from ADR-023's amendments of 2026-10-13 and 2026-10-15, moved 2026-11-08)*
Lessons that passed before they could be cancelled — to the coach, when a stuck schedule change finishes after some of
  its lessons' times: "These lessons were due to be cancelled, but their time passed before the cancellation could be
  applied." The coach can waive them and contact the families. (ADR-010)
  *(from ADR-010 §5i, moved 2026-11-08: the family was not told and may have turned up; the coach is told in the
  batch's notification.)*

